2026-09-18T12:59:19.6199054Z [36;1m# re-runs only that suite's failed tests -- across ALL lit failure[0m
2026-09-18T12:59:19.6199547Z [36;1m# labels (FAIL/TIMEOUT/UNRESOLVED/XPASS), so a real non-FAIL failure is[0m
2026-09-18T12:59:19.6200040Z [36;1m# never dropped. For an EIO (which can abort lit mid-suite, leaving[0m
2026-09-18T12:59:19.6200629Z [36;1m# tests un-run) it re-runs the failed suite in FULL. Suites the[0m
2026-09-18T12:59:19.6201103Z [36;1m# fail-fast pass never reached always run in full. So every test that[0m
2026-09-18T12:59:19.6201581Z [36;1m# ran in the baseline still runs, and any deterministic failure fails[0m
